{"title":"Career Roadmap: Electrical Engineer","role":"Electrical Engineer","summary":"An Electrical Engineer can work across several areas rather than following one narrow specialization.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Electrical Engineering"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Design, operate, maintain, analyze and improve electrical power and energy systems, equipment and industrial electrical infrastructure"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Electrical Engineer can work across several areas rather than following one narrow specialization."},{"type":"p","text":"The major career directions include:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Power Systems","Electrical Machines","Power Electronics","Control & Automation","Renewable Energy","EVs","Industrial Electrical Systems","Smart Grids"]},{"type":"p","text":"The undergraduate roadmap should therefore establish broad electrical fundamentals in the first two years and then develop a specialization + practical engineering portfolio during the final two years."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Progress","Gap It Moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"1st Year"},{"text":"Circuit theory, mathematics, programming and basic electronics"},{"text":"MIT OpenCourseWare · NPTEL","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/"},{"text":"Circuit simulations + programming projects"},{"text":"Electrical foundation"}],[{"text":"2nd Year"},{"text":"Machines, measurements, power electronics and control"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Machine/control simulations + laboratory projects"},{"text":"Core electrical engineering"}],[{"text":"3rd Year"},{"text":"Power systems, protection, automation and electrical design"},{"text":"IEC Standards","url":"https://www.iec.ch/standards"},{"text":"Power-system studies + electrical design"},{"text":"Industry readiness"}],[{"text":"4th Year"},{"text":"Specialization + industrial project + internship"},{"text":"IEEE Standards Association","url":"https://standards.ieee.org/"},{"text":"Major capstone + internship"},{"text":"Professional specialization"}]]}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Semester","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Sem 1"},{"text":"Engineering mathematics, basic electrical engineering, programming"}],[{"text":"Sem 2"},{"text":"Circuit theory, electronics, electrical measurements"}],[{"text":"Sem 3"},{"text":"Electrical machines, signals and systems, digital electronics"}],[{"text":"Sem 4"},{"text":"Power electronics, control systems, microprocessors"}],[{"text":"Sem 5"},{"text":"Power systems, switchgear and protection"}],[{"text":"Sem 6"},{"text":"Electrical design, instrumentation, automation"}],[{"text":"Sem 7"},{"text":"Specialization + industrial applications"}],[{"text":"Sem 8"},{"text":"Capstone + internship/job preparation"}]]}]},{"heading":"Core Electrical Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Circuit Theory"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ohm's law"},{"text":"Kirchhoff's laws"},{"text":"AC/DC circuits"},{"text":"impedance"},{"text":"admittance"},{"text":"resonance"},{"text":"power factor"},{"text":"three-phase systems"},{"text":"active/reactive/apparent power"}]},{"type":"p","text":"You should be comfortable calculating:"},{"type":"p","text":"P, Q, S, power factor and three-phase loads."}]},{"heading":"Electrical Machines","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Transformers"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"transformer operation"},{"text":"equivalent circuits"},{"text":"efficiency"},{"text":"regulation"},{"text":"losses"},{"text":"three-phase transformers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Motors"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"induct